From: Celestials316 <240407887+Celestials316@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:06:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deps,v8: spell out the 128-bit ShuffleArray type

Node 27's alpha V8 declares ShuffleArray as an alias template, then
default-constructs it without template arguments. The Android host
toolchain used for node_js2c rejects alias-template CTAD, so name the
existing default width explicitly. This is a build fix with no runtime
or data-layout change.
---
 deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/wasm-shuffle-reducer.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/wasm-shuffle-reducer.cc b/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/wasm-shuffle-reducer.cc
index 5938a6dd34..0597712d8c 100644
--- a/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/wasm-shuffle-reducer.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/wasm-shuffle-reducer.cc
@@ -853,7 +853,7 @@ void WasmShuffleAnalyzer::ProcessShuffleOfLoads(const Simd128ShuffleOp& shuffle,
 
   if (GetDemandedBytes(&shuffle).IsAll()) {
     // Full width shuffles.
-    SimdShuffle::ShuffleArray shuffle_bytes;
+    SimdShuffle::ShuffleArray<kSimd128Size> shuffle_bytes;
     std::copy_n(shuffle.shuffle.begin(), kSimd128Size, shuffle_bytes.begin());
     auto canonical = SimdShuffle::TryMatchCanonical(shuffle_bytes);
     switch (canonical) {
